<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $84.8 mln April 23.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $84.8 mln April 23.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $84.8 million surplus on April 23 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 23</p>
<p>Exports: $416.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $283.9 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $149.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $197 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $84.8 million</p>
<p>APRIL DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.597 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.707 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.422 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.834 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $478 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
